From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:59:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] vkd3d: place a resource where its Vulkan memory allows

MultiVersus (Unreal Engine 5.1, Direct3D 12) places resources in its
transient heaps at offsets that are not multiples of their 64 KiB
placement alignment: a 256 KiB UAV buffer at 0x8000, a 1564x720
depth-stencil texture at 0x48000. CreatePlacedResource returned
E_INVALIDARG, and the engine stopped with "hr failed at
D3D12Resources.cpp:391 with error E_INVALIDARG" (a GPUCrash in its crash
report) at a random point, 45 to 80 s into the title screen or on its
first button press.

Place such a resource when the Vulkan memory allows the offset, with a
fixme the first time: a buffer, a slice of the heap's own VkBuffer, at
any multiple of the 256 bytes vkd3d-proton already gives a buffer with
tight alignment; a single-sampled texture at a multiple of 4 KiB that
its image's own memory alignment also divides (checked once the image
exists, and the call still fails if not). Anything else still fails.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-30-d3d12-feature-level-12.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 libs/vkd3d/resource.c | 37 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libs/vkd3d/resource.c b/libs/vkd3d/resource.c
index a8fc26b..9c3d0ab 100644
--- a/libs/vkd3d/resource.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/resource.c
@@ -4645,6 +4645,7 @@ HRESULT d3d12_resource_create_placed(struct d3d12_device *device, const D3D12_RE
     VKD3D_UNUSED VkDeviceSize required_size;
     VkBindImageMemoryInfo bind_info;
     struct d3d12_resource *object;
+    bool offset_relaxed;
     VkResult vr;
     HRESULT hr;
 
@@ -4696,12 +4697,32 @@ HRESULT d3d12_resource_create_placed(struct d3d12_device *device, const D3D12_RE
         goto fail;
     }
 
+    /* Unreal Engine 5.1's transient allocator places resources at offsets that
+     * are not multiples of their 64 KiB placement alignment (MultiVersus: a
+     * 256 KiB UAV buffer at 0x8000, a 1564x720 depth-stencil texture at
+     * 0x48000), and treats the failed call as fatal. Where the Vulkan memory
+     * allows the offset, place the resource there instead: a buffer is a range
+     * of the heap's own buffer and needs the 256 bytes tight alignment gives
+     * buffers; a single-sampled texture needs its image's own alignment, which
+     * is checked below once the image exists. */
+    offset_relaxed = false;
     if (heap_offset & (object->placed_alignment - 1u))
     {
-        WARN("Heap offset %#"PRIx64" not a multiple of resource alignment %#"PRIx64".\n",
-                heap_offset, object->placed_alignment);
-        hr = E_INVALIDARG;
-        goto fail;
+        if ((d3d12_resource_is_buffer(object) && !(heap_offset & (VKD3D_MIN_BUFFER_ALIGNMENT - 1u))) ||
+                (d3d12_resource_is_texture(object) && desc->SampleDesc.Count == 1 &&
+                        !(heap_offset & (D3D12_SMALL_RESOURCE_PLACEMENT_ALIGNMENT - 1u))))
+        {
+            FIXME_ONCE("Placing a resource at heap offset %#"PRIx64", not a multiple of its alignment %#"PRIx64".\n",
+                    heap_offset, object->placed_alignment);
+            offset_relaxed = true;
+        }
+        else
+        {
+            WARN("Heap offset %#"PRIx64" not a multiple of resource alignment %#"PRIx64".\n",
+                    heap_offset, object->placed_alignment);
+            hr = E_INVALIDARG;
+            goto fail;
+        }
     }
 
     if (d3d12_resource_is_texture(object))
@@ -4712,6 +4733,14 @@ HRESULT d3d12_resource_create_placed(struct d3d12_device *device, const D3D12_RE
         /* Align manually. This works because we padded the required allocation size reported to the app. */
         VK_CALL(vkGetImageMemoryRequirements(device->vk_device, object->res.vk_image, &memory_requirements));
 
+        if (offset_relaxed && ((heap->allocation.offset + heap_offset) & (memory_requirements.alignment - 1)))
+        {
+            WARN("Heap offset %#"PRIx64" not a multiple of image alignment %#"PRIx64".\n",
+                    heap_offset, (uint64_t)memory_requirements.alignment);
+            hr = E_INVALIDARG;
+            goto fail;
+        }
+
         /* For SMALL_RESOURCE_PLACEMENT when we have workaround active,
          * verify that application did in fact check alignment requirements.
          * If application places 64k aligned, we will have made sure to leave room for padding below.
